# DROP — copy to .env and fill in real values. Never commit a real .env.
# Google OAuth (Google Cloud Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials)
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID is the PUBLIC client ID used by Google Identity
# Services in the browser. DROP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID is the same value, read
# server-side by the /api/auth/google function to verify ID tokens.
# Set both to the same client ID in Vercel (Production) and redeploy.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
DROP_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# Shared user tracking (Neon Postgres, 2026-11-19) — optional, but
# required to see how many users signed up. Without it, profiles live
# only in each browser's localStorage and there is no central count.
# Create a free project at https://neon.tech → New Project → copy the
# connection string (it starts postgres://... and ends with
# ?sslmode=require). Set it in Vercel → Settings → Environment
# Variables as a Secret for Production, then redeploy. Never commit a
# real connection string — it is a password.
DATABASE_URL=
# Optional: extra admin emails allowed to see Admin → user insights,
# comma-separated. Defaults to the owner: durgaprasadt235@gmail.com.
# DROP_ADMIN_EMAILS=
# Avatar / cover uploads (Page 04, optional) — Vercel Blob. Create a Blob
# store in Vercel (Storage → Create → Blob), then set its token as a
# Secret for Production and redeploy. Without it, photo upload returns
# 503 and the app honestly says storage is not configured; the Google
# photo or initials avatar is used instead. Never commit a real token.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
# Phone + OTP is DISABLED (2026-11-19) — no Twilio variables are used.
# Do not add DROP_TWILIO_*; the phone sign-in, OTP and phone-based
# password reset were removed from the client and the server.
